PERFORMANCE AND QUARTER TRENDS,

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.527
WHICH ARE IN OUR BOARD AGENDAS

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.563
ONLINE. HOWEVER, WE'RE WORKING

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.631
TO SYNTHESIZE THIS INFORMATION

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.432
AND PUT IT UP ON OUR WEBSITE TO

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.600
BE MORE READILY AVAILABLE AND

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:59.105
ACCESSIBLE TO THE PUBLIC. MOVING

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.973
ON TO THE NEXT SLIDE, I WANTED

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.576
TO GET INTO SOME OF THE DATA

00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:05.311
AROUND ACHIEVING OUR ON TIME

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.412
PERFORMANCE GOALS. THIS CHART

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:08.347
SHOWS DELAYS BY RESPONSIBLE

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:11.050
PARTY PER 10,000 TRAIN MILES,

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:12.919
BUT I REALLY WANTED TO HIGHLIGHT

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.120
REALLY THE TOP FIVE DELAY TYPES

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:15.554
THAT WE SEE FOR PACIFIC

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.556
SURFLINER. AND THOSE DELAY TYPES

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:18.724
INCLUDE PASSENGER TRAIN

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:19.292
INTERFERENCE, SIGNAL DELAYS,

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:22.128
COMMUTER TRAIN INTERFERENCE,

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:23.095
PASSENGER RELATED DELAYS, AND

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:25.364
SLOW ORDERS. I WANTED TO TOUCH

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.233
UPON A COUPLE OF THESE AREAS

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.935
BRIEFLY. I WANTED TO TOUCH UPON

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:29.969
PASSENGER TRAIN INTERFERENCE.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.470
THIS IS REALLY WHEN ANOTHER

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.873
AMTRAK TRAIN IS OUT OF ITS

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:34.907
SCHEDULED SLOT, AND CREATES A

00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:36.008
DELAY TO ANOTHER PACIFIC

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.077
SURFLINER TRAIN. THIS COULD BE

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:40.313
CAUSED BY A SERIES OF DIFFERENT

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:41.280
ISSUES RELATED TO MECHANICAL

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.382
DELAYS, EVEN PASSENGER RELATED

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:44.417
DELAYS, OR ANYTHING ELSE THAT

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:46.452
COULD INITIALLY DELAY A

00:09:46.519 --> 00:09:48.821
SURFLINER TRAIN IN ROUTE. THIS

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:49.822
IS TYPICALLY ASSOCIATED WITH

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:52.325
CASCADING DELAYS FROM ANOTHER

00:09:52.391 --> 00:09:54.860
SOURCE, AND GIVEN THE WIDE, WIDE

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:56.028
RANGE OF ROOT CAUSES FOR THIS

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:58.331
TYPE OF DELAY, THERE ISN'T A

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.398
SINGLE APPROACH REALLY TO

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.100
ADDRESSING IT. STAFF CONTINUES

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:02.234
TO WORK WITH OUR HOST RAILROADS

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:04.170
ON DISPATCHING PRIORITIES TO

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:08.941
MINIMIZE THESE TYPES OF DELAYS, WE ALSO WORK WITH OUR AMTRAK

00:10:09.008 --> 00:10:10.276
MECHANICAL TEAM TO IDENTIFY

00:10:10.343 --> 00:10:11.210
ROUTE MECHANICAL ISSUES, TO

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:13.212
REALLY TRY TO LIMIT ISSUES THAT

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.748
COULD CREATE AN INITIAL DELAY.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:16.949
SOME OF THE OTHER DELAYS THAT I

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:18.250
WANTED TO QUICKLY MENTION ARE

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:19.318
SIGNAL DELAYS. NOW, THESE ARE

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:21.220
OFTEN CAUSED BY SIGNAL

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:21.821
MALFUNCTIONS, WHICH SOMETIMES

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:24.390
COULD BE A SIMPLE FAILURE OF A

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:26.192
PART. BUT MOST RECENTLY, WHICH I

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:28.461
THINK DARREN MAY GET INTO AS

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:30.196
PART OF HIS DISCUSSION, IS

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:30.696
VANDALISM, WHERE THERE'S

00:10:30.763 --> 00:10:31.497
ACTUALLY THIEVES TAKING THE

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:34.133
COPPER COMMUNICATION WIRING FROM

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.435
THE CONTROL BOXES, WHICH

00:10:36.502 --> 00:10:37.003
OBVIOUSLY CAUSES SIGNIFICANT

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:40.673
DISRUPTIONS. ALSO, A LOT OF OUR

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.508
SIGNAL DELAYS HAVE BEEN TIED TO

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:43.609
CHALLENGES BEING FACED ON THE

00:10:43.676 --> 00:10:45.611
NORTHERN END OF OUR CORRIDOR

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:46.712
RELATED TO GRADE CROSSINGS. NOW,

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:49.515
THIS ISSUE IS WHERE THE TRAINS

00:10:49.582 --> 00:10:51.083
ARE NOT CONSISTENTLY ACTIVATING

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.051
CROSSINGS WITH THE APPROPRIATE

00:10:52.118 --> 00:10:54.620
AMOUNT OF LEAD TIME. THIS IS

00:10:54.687 --> 00:10:55.821
KNOWN AS A SHUNTING ISSUE, AND

00:10:55.888 --> 00:10:57.289
TO MAINTAIN SAFETY WHILE

00:10:57.356 --> 00:10:58.290
OPERATING, THE RAILROADS HAVE

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:00.426
IMPLEMENTED SLOW ORDERS AT THESE

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:02.161
CROSSINGS TO AVOID THE POTENTIAL

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:03.662
OF A STRIKE. A LONG TERM

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.297
SOLUTION HAS BEEN IDENTIFIED TO

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:08.034
INSTALL AN ANTENNA ON THE TRUCKS

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.235
OF BOTH THE LOCOMOTIVE AND THE

00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:11.137
CAB CONTROL CARS, WHICH

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:12.038
BASICALLY ENHANCES THE

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.040
ELECTRICAL SIGNAL BETWEEN THE

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:16.675
RAILS THAT ALLOW THE CIRCUIT

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:17.676
CONTROLLING THE CROSSING TO

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:19.645
SHUNT MORE RELIABLY. SO WE ARE

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:22.114
EXCITED ABOUT A TEST OF THIS

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:23.215
PROTOTYPE ANTENNA IS SCHEDULED

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:26.285
WITH UNION PACIFIC ON THE LOW

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:28.254
SAN CORRIDOR FOR SEPTEMBER, BUT

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.157
UNTIL THAT POSSIBLE FIX IS

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:32.291
IMPLEMENTED, WE WILL CONTINUE TO

00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:35.227
SEE THESE THESE TYPES OF DELAYS

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:36.429
UP IN THE NORTHERN END OF OUR

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:41.634
CORRIDOR. MOVING ON TO SLIDE

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.769
EIGHT. NOW, I WANTED TO TALK

00:11:43.836 --> 00:11:44.937
ABOUT ANOTHER TOPIC THAT CAUSES

00:11:45.004 --> 00:11:46.705
DELAYS AND THAT IS THE

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:47.706
UNFORTUNATE INCIDENT OF

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:49.775
TRESPASSER STRIKES. THIS SLIDE

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.944
SHOWS THE TRENDS AROUND

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:52.945
TRESPASSER STRIKES AND VEHICLE

00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:54.880
STRIKES FOR PACIFIC SURFLINER.

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:56.782
SINCE FEDERAL FISCAL YEAR 20

00:11:56.849 --> 00:11:59.585
1819, A FEW KEY PIECES OF

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:00.686
INFORMATION I WANTED TO POINT

00:12:00.753 --> 00:12:01.921
OUT IS THAT IN FEDERAL FISCAL

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:04.390
YEAR 24, 68% OF STRIKES HAVE

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:06.092
BEEN TRESPASSERS, WHILE 32% ARE

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:08.661
VEHICLES, 95% OF FATAL STRIKES

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:11.063
HAVE BEEN TRESPASSERS, AND 86%

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.899
OF TRESPASSER STRIKES HAVE NOT

00:12:13.966 --> 00:12:15.601
BEEN AT A CROSSING. SO 95% OF

00:12:15.668 --> 00:12:19.171
TRESPASSER STRIKES HAVE BEEN

00:12:19.238 --> 00:12:23.242
FATAL, AND OR EXCUSE ME, 95% OF

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:24.577
THE FATAL STRIKES HAVE BEEN

00:12:24.643 --> 00:12:25.644
TRESPASSERS, STRIKES ARE

00:12:25.711 --> 00:12:27.713
TYPICALLY HIGHER DURING WINTER

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.482
MONTHS LIKE WE SAW THIS PAST

00:12:29.548 --> 00:12:31.584
JANUARY. I DO WANT TO MENTION

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.552
THAT WE ALSO PROVIDE A QUARTERLY

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:36.155
REPORT TO OUR BOARD ON THE

00:12:36.222 --> 00:12:37.289
SYSTEM SAFETY. THAT DOES INCLUDE

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:39.358
DETAILS ON TRESPASSER STRIKES,

00:12:39.425 --> 00:12:41.193
AND WE ARE LOOKING TO MAKE THIS

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.661
INFORMATION ALSO MORE READILY

00:12:42.728 --> 00:12:43.696
AVAILABLE ON OUR WEBSITE. IN

00:12:43.762 --> 00:12:45.764
ADDITION TO THE QUARTER TRENDS,

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:48.067
INFORMATION THAT I SPOKE ABOUT,

00:12:48.134 --> 00:12:50.803
WE DO RECOGNIZE THE IMPACTS THAT

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.837
THESE TRESPASSER STRIKES HAVE ON

00:12:51.904 --> 00:12:53.305
OUR CUSTOMERS AND OUR

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:55.608
OPERATIONS. AND THIS ISN'T

00:12:55.674 --> 00:12:56.775
REALLY A ONE SIZE FITS ALL

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:58.344
SOLUTION. WE HAVE RECENTLY

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.178
COORDINATED WITH CALIFORNIA

00:12:59.245 --> 00:13:01.580
OPERATION LIFESAVER ON OPERATION

00:13:01.647 --> 00:13:04.283
SAFE SURF INITIATIVE, WHICH IS A

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:04.817
MULTIFACETED STRATEGY FOR

00:13:04.884 --> 00:13:07.219
ENHANCED RAIL SAFETY, EDUCATION

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:08.254
AND AWARENESS. AS PART OF THIS,

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.556
WE HAVE RECENTLY COMPLETED RAIL

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:11.190
SAFETY ADVERTISEMENTS DISPLAYED

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:13.526
ON INTERNET CONNECTED TVS AND

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:15.995
STREAMING PLATFORMS THROUGHOUT

00:13:16.061 --> 00:13:17.062
AREAS ON THE CORRIDOR WHERE

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:18.697
INCIDENTS ARE MOST PREVALENT.

00:13:18.764 --> 00:13:21.333
THESE AREAS INCLUDE SOLANA BEACH

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.334
AND OCEANSIDE, LÀ, TÊ,

00:13:22.401 --> 00:13:24.470
FULLERTON, OXNARD, AND

00:13:24.537 --> 00:13:25.571
CAMARILLO, AS WELL AS SANTA

00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:27.806
BARBARA. WE ALSO HAVE DONE

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:28.707
GEOFENCE SAFETY MESSAGING

00:13:28.774 --> 00:13:30.676
DISTRIBUTED THROUGH CELL PHONE

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:31.677
ADVERTISING. WE ARE CURRENTLY

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:33.312
WORKING ON DESIGNING SIGNAGE TO

00:13:33.379 --> 00:13:34.980
BE INSTALLED ALONG HIGH RISK

00:13:35.047 --> 00:13:37.383
AREAS OF THE CORRIDOR, AND THEN

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:39.185
THE FINAL LEG OF THE PROGRAM IS

00:13:39.251 --> 00:13:40.319
TO ENGAGE WITH LOCAL RESOURCES

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:42.321
ALONG THE CORRIDOR FOR

00:13:42.388 --> 00:13:43.355
OPPORTUNITIES THAT THEY MAY BE

00:13:43.422 --> 00:13:45.524
ABLE TO HELP PROVIDE OUTREACH TO

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:46.659
INDIVIDUALS THAT ARE LIVING NEAR

00:13:46.725 --> 00:13:48.227
THE TRACKS TO OFFER RAIL SAFETY

00:13:48.294 --> 00:13:50.829
INFORMATION AND RESOURCES. WE'RE

00:13:50.896 --> 00:13:54.099
ALSO CURRENTLY LOOKING TO GET

00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:55.167
PSA EDUCATIONAL VIDEOS AND

00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:57.069
INFORMATION OUT TO LOCAL

00:13:57.136 --> 00:13:58.137
GOVERNMENT JURISDICTIONS WHO

00:13:58.204 --> 00:14:00.105
HAVE LOCAL BROADCAST CHANNELS,

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:03.008
REALLY TO GET A BROADER REACH

00:14:03.075 --> 00:14:05.444
OUT TO OUR LOCAL REGIONS AND

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:06.512
FINALLY, WE ARE LOOKING AT

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:07.880
TECHNOLOGICAL OPPORTUNITIES TO

00:14:07.947 --> 00:14:10.549
PILOT THAT INCLUDE TRACK

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:11.050
INTRUSION AND DETECTION

00:14:11.116 --> 00:14:12.551
SOLUTIONS, AND WE LOOK FORWARD

00:14:12.618 --> 00:14:14.086
TO COORDINATING WITH NCTD,

00:14:14.153 --> 00:14:16.488
METROLINK AND UP ON THESE

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:17.723
POSSIBLE SOLUTIONS, I DID WANT

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.659
TO MENTION ONE LAST ITEM, AND

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.394
THAT IS THAT WE ALSO HAVE

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:23.395
COORDINATED WITH AMTRAK POLICE

00:14:23.462 --> 00:14:25.864
DEPARTMENT ON EMERGENCY RESPONSE

00:14:25.931 --> 00:14:26.665
TRAINING FOR TRESPASSER

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:28.734
INCIDENTS IN WHICH THEY HAVE

00:14:28.801 --> 00:14:29.802
DEVELOPED TRAINING CLASSES AS

00:14:29.868 --> 00:14:31.837
PART OF A STATEWIDE TRAINING FOR

00:14:31.904 --> 00:14:34.340
FIRST RESPONDERS AND CORONERS ON

00:14:34.406 --> 00:14:35.441
HOW TO REALLY DEAL WITH

00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:37.443
TRESPASSER STRIKES AND REALLY

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:38.410
RAIL EMERGENCIES. AND THIS

00:14:38.477 --> 00:14:39.278
TRAINING IS PLANNED TO BE ROLLED

00:14:39.345 --> 00:14:45.284
OUT THIS YEAR. OKAY, NOW I

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:48.120
WANTED TO CHANGE GEARS A LITTLE

00:14:48.187 --> 00:14:49.989
BIT AND TALK ABOUT OUR ANNUAL

00:14:50.055 --> 00:14:51.123
BUSINESS PLAN PROCESS, UNDER OUR

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:54.360
INTERAGENCY TRANSFER AGREEMENT

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:55.427
BETWEEN THE AGENCY AND THE

00:14:55.494 --> 00:14:57.162
STATE, THE AGENCY IS REQUIRED TO

00:14:57.229 --> 00:14:58.330
SUBMIT AN ANNUAL BUSINESS PLAN.

00:14:58.397 --> 00:15:01.233
I'M GOING TO REFER TO IT AS OUR

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.234
AVP, TO THE CALIFORNIA

00:15:02.301 --> 00:15:03.335
TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY BY

00:15:03.402 --> 00:15:06.038
APRIL 1ST OF EACH YEAR. AND OUR

00:15:06.105 --> 00:15:07.072
AGREEMENT WITH THE STATE

00:15:07.139 --> 00:15:09.441
PRESCRIBES ELEMENTS OF THE AVP,

00:15:09.508 --> 00:15:10.676
WHICH IS A TWO YEAR PLANNING,

00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:12.778
OPERATIONS AND BUDGET DOCUMENT

00:15:12.845 --> 00:15:13.746
AND SERVES REALLY AS THE

00:15:13.812 --> 00:15:15.281
AGENCY'S PLAN FOR OPERATING THE

00:15:15.347 --> 00:15:16.282
PACIFIC SURFLINER INTERCITY RAIL

00:15:16.348 --> 00:15:18.951
SERVICE. IT ALSO INCLUDES A

00:15:19.018 --> 00:15:20.119
REPORT ON OVERALL PERFORMANCE,

00:15:20.185 --> 00:15:21.287
MARKETING PLAN, CAPITAL

00:15:21.353 --> 00:15:22.221
IMPROVEMENT PROJECTS ALONG THE

00:15:22.288 --> 00:15:24.423
CORRIDOR AND INCLUDES THE

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.092
AGENCY'S FUNDING REQUESTS FOR

00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:27.693
ADMINISTRATION, OPERATIONS AND

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:31.096
MARKETING. THIS PAST YEAR, WE

00:15:31.163 --> 00:15:31.597
BEGAN INCORPORATING THE

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:34.233
REQUIREMENTS OF SB 677 INTO OUR

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.135
AVP, WHICH INCLUDES A DISCUSSION

00:15:36.201 --> 00:15:37.903
ON THE EFFECTS OF CLIMATE CHANGE

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.605
ON THE CORRIDOR, AS WELL AS IT

00:15:39.672 --> 00:15:41.307
HIGHLIGHTS CAPITAL PROJECTS

00:15:41.373 --> 00:15:42.374
PLANNED ALONG THE CORRIDOR TO

00:15:42.441 --> 00:15:44.576
INCREASE RESILIENCY AND RELATED

00:15:44.643 --> 00:15:45.444
FUNDING OPPORTUNITIES IDENTIFIED

00:15:45.511 --> 00:15:50.349
FOR EACH PROJECT. AND THE AVP

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:53.152
PROCESS ITSELF IS REALLY A SIX

00:15:53.218 --> 00:15:54.887
MONTH PROCESS THAT STARTS WITH

00:15:54.953 --> 00:15:56.755
OUR AGENCY DEVELOPING KEY

00:15:56.822 --> 00:15:58.657
ASSUMPTIONS THAT ARE REVIEWED BY

00:15:58.724 --> 00:15:59.658
OUR TECHNICAL ADVISORY COMMITTEE

